SDCC - free open source, retargettable, optimizing ISO C compiler
------------------------------------------------------------------

Please see doc/README.txt for the upstream documentation index.  MCS-251
target notes are in doc/mcs251/README.md.  The parallel Simplified Chinese
manual for SDCC, MCS-51 and MCS-251 is in doc/zh-CN/README.md.  All project
documentation is kept below doc/; there is no separate docs/ tree.


Building from source
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The normal build keeps generated files outside the source tree.  The
MCS-51 port is enabled by default.  The MCS-251 port is experimental and
must be selected explicitly with --enable-mcs251-port.

On Debian or Ubuntu, install the host build dependencies with:

    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get install build-essential bison flex gputils libboost-dev \
        libreadline-dev texinfo zlib1g-dev

On macOS, install the Xcode command-line tools, then install the parser
generators and Boost.  Make sure the Homebrew bison and flex executables
come before the system versions in PATH:

    xcode-select --install
    brew install bison boost flex gputils gnu-sed readline texinfo
    export PATH="$(brew --prefix bison)/bin:$(brew --prefix flex)/bin:$PATH"

Clone and configure both MCS-51 and MCS-251 support:

    git clone https://github.com/zevorn/sdcc-c251.git
    cd sdcc-c251
    mkdir build
    cd build
    CFLAGS=-std=gnu17 ../configure \
        --enable-mcs251-port --prefix="$PWD/install"

On macOS, Homebrew installs Boost outside the compiler's default header
search path.  Use this configure form instead:

    CFLAGS=-std=gnu17 \
    CPPFLAGS="-I$(brew --prefix boost)/include" \
    ../configure \
        --enable-mcs251-port --prefix="$PWD/install"

The default configuration also builds the other maintained SDCC ports,
assemblers, linkers, device headers, run-time libraries, packihx, sdcdb and
ucSim.  Inspect all available switches with ../configure --help.  To leave
out an unneeded target, pass its --disable-<target>-port option.

Build and install into build/install:

    make -j4
    make install

The explicit CFLAGS setting is required because parts of the inherited
ASxxxx sources still use K&R function definitions that C23 rejects.  It
changes only the host compiler mode; it does not change the C dialect
accepted by SDCC.


Verifying the build
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Check the installed compiler and the two target names:

    install/bin/sdcc --version
    grep -E '^(mcs51|mcs251)$' ports.build

Run the compiler and code-generation checks for MCS-251, then make sure the
shared MCS-51 path still compiles its regression program:

    make -C src/mcs251 check
    bin/sdcc -mmcs51 -I../device/include -S \
        -o /tmp/mcs51-smoke.asm \
        ../src/mcs251/tests/mcs51-regression.c

The complete MCS-251 library build produces these four ABI-matched library
directories below device/lib/build/:

    mcs251-small
    mcs251-small-stack-auto
    mcs251-large
    mcs251-large-stack-auto


Running with QEMU
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The QEMU checks require the MCS-251 and MCS-51 system emulators from the
companion QEMU tree.  From the SDCC build directory, run:

    make -C src/mcs251 check-qemu \
        QEMU_MCS251=/path/to/qemu-system-mcs251

    make -C src/mcs251 check-mcs51-qemu \
        QEMU_MCS51=/path/to/qemu-system-mcs51

The first target covers MCS-251 runtime, memory-model, optimization, official
example-derived and GDB-stub checks.  The second target verifies that the
MCS-51 object and runtime baseline remains unchanged.  A full MCS-251
regression run is available through:

    make -C support/regression test-mcs251 \
        QEMU_MCS251=/path/to/qemu-system-mcs251

Use the QEMU trace and GDB-stub procedures in doc/mcs251/debugging.md when a
runtime check fails.  If generated code and ABI evidence are correct, first
exclude a QEMU defect before changing the mature MCS-51-compatible paths.


Building the documentation
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The upstream English manual keeps its original LyX layout under doc/.  Build
it by configuring SDCC with --enable-doc and running the normal make target.
The Simplified Chinese PDF and HTML are independent outputs in the same doc/
tree:

    make -C doc/zh-CN check all

See doc/zh-CN/README.md for the Pandoc, XeLaTeX and CJK font dependencies.
